codex
The implementation now retains the staged directory descriptor across the atomic rename, seals that exact inode, and resolves the live name read-only afterward. If another publisher replaced the name, it compares the two pinned entries byte-for-byte and returns reuse or conflict; it no longer seals a replacement by name. I’m smoke-testing this shape before adding the forced interleaving regressions.
